\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/ksrv.fam — what the kernel does for programs: the store, the console and
\ exec, as requests served by the loop thread.
\
\   ksinit ( -- )      once, after stinit and exinit
\   ksturn ( -- )      once per loop turn: serve every pending request; flush
\                      buffered output that is full, 100 ms old, or whose
\                      thread is gone
\   kserve ( tid -- )  serve that thread's request (what ksturn does per thread)
\   kflush ( tid -- )  append what that thread has buffered to its bound key
\
\ A request (lib/sys.fam kreq: syscall D) is five words in the thread's record
\ (src/proc.fam: +64 op, +68..+74 a b c d, +78 the reply, +7C 1 pending,
\ 2 answered); the thread waits for event bit 17 and thread 0 is posted bit 16.
\   1 get    ( key klen buf cap -- vlen | -1 none )
\   2 put    ( key klen data n -- 0 )
\   3 append ( key klen data n -- 0 )
\   4 del    ( key klen -- -1 | 0 )
\   5 exec   ( key klen size tickets -- tid | 0 )
\   6 bind   ( proto port ring size -- 0 | -1 taken | -3 full )   src/ports.fam
\   7 unbind ( proto port -- 0 )
\   8 txring ( ring size -- 0 )   the thread's transmit ring: frames put in it
\            go out when the loop thread next turns (post it bit 19)
\   9 netinfo ( buf -- 0 )   24 bytes into buf: ip, mask, gateway, its MAC, ours
\   B read   ( key klen blk -- n | -1 none )   bytes of the value from an
\            offset: blk is three words in the program, buf, cap, offset; n
\            is what was copied, 0 at the end
\   C watch  ( key klen -- 0 | -1 full )   be posted bit 20 whenever that key
\            is written (put, append, or a console flush into it); 32 watches
\   D unwatch ( key klen -- 0 )
\   E kill   ( tid -- 0 | -1 gone | -2 )   end that thread (exit code 9); not
\            thread 0 or oneself
\   F rewind ( key klen -- 0 )   the key's input cursor to its start, and the
\            key read as a file: a reader at its end gets 0 (a shell's "<");
\            otherwise a key is a pipe and a reader at its end waits
\   10, 11   the loop thread's side of the UART emulation (src/proc.fam kuart):
\            fill a thread's input buffer from its input, flush its output
\   12 halt  ( -- )   the node stops (the console shell's exit)
\   A scan   ( start slen buf cap -- n )   the keys from start on, in order, as
\            many as fit cap: records of klen, vlen (words), the key and the
\            value's first 64 bytes, each padded to 4.  An iterator: the
\            caller stops at the first key it does not want and continues from
\            the last one it got followed by a 0 byte
\ Any pointer outside the requester's own region and its process's: -2.  Each
\ store request is a transaction of its own.
\
\ The key proc/self/args is the thread's arguments (a line, at most 255 bytes):
\ put sets them, get reads them, a child starts with its parent's.  A shell
\ sets them to the command line before the exec and clears them after.
\ Keys are paths.  A thread has a working directory (the key ".": get reads
\ it, put sets it, "/" to start with, a child's is its parent's at exec), and
\ a key is resolved before the store sees it: one starting with "/" is taken
\ from the root, any other is the working directory, "/" and the key.  The
\ tree's keys have no leading slash, so "/bin/init" is the key bin/init.
\ A resolved key over 511 bytes is refused (-1, or 0 from del and exec).  The
\ kernel only joins: "." and ".." in a key are names like any other, a shell
\ resolves them before asking.  exec of a name without a slash runs bin/NAME.
\
\ Handles.  The key "0" is the program's console.  put and append write the
\ bytes to the UART or, when its output is bound, add them to a value in the
\ store; get reads what has arrived on the UART, or the next bytes of the value
\ its input is bound to, from a cursor the key's readers share (so a child
\ reading the pipe its parent reads goes on from where the parent was, and the
\ parent from where the child left off; a put or del of the key starts it
\ over).  Either way a get with nothing to read
\ stays pending and is served when there is: a UART byte (its interrupt is
\ armed while a program waits for one), or a write to the bound key.  The key
\ "1" is the output binding, "2" the input binding: put a key (up to 63 bytes)
\ to bind, an empty value to bind back to the console; get gives it.  A program
\ starts with its parent's bindings (handed to the child as it is spawned).
\ Bytes for a bound output are buffered, 1 KiB per thread, and appended when
\ the buffer is full, 100 ms old, 0 is rebound, 0 is read, or the thread is
\ gone, so the value lags by at most that.  Two programs joined by a key, one
\ writing it as its output and one reading it as its input, are a pipe; a
\ program that watches a key is told of every write to it, which is how the
\ window manager relays a shell's output as it appears (lib/pterm.fam).
\ Needs src/exec.fam, src/ports.fam (and what they need) and src/tcp.fam's tms.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: ksbt variable ;                                 \ 16 x 0x820: +0 output buffer (0x400) +400 fill +404 stamp (ms) +408 input fill +40C waiting for input +410 input position +414 input at its end +418 input buffer (0x400)
: kscr variable ;  : kscd variable ;               \ the input cursors (32 x 0x50: +0 klen, 0 free; +4 cursor; +8 key; +48 a file: reads end at its end): one per key, shared by its readers
: kswt variable ;  : ksagain variable ;  : ksuw variable ;   \ the watches (32 x 0x40: +0 tid +4 klen +8 key), serve again, a UART reader waits
: kst variable ;  : kso variable ;  : ks1 variable ;  : ks2 variable ;  : ks3 variable ;  : ks4 variable ;
: ksp variable ;  : ksl variable ;  : ksk variable ;                  \ ksk: the resolved key (0x200)

: ksbuf ( tid -- rec )  820 lit * ksbt @ + ;
: ksinit ( -- )  8200 lit alloc dup ksbt !  2080 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop  ksbt @ K 44 lit + !  200 lit alloc ksk !
	800 lit alloc dup kswt !  200 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop  0 lit ksuw !
	A00 lit alloc dup kscr !  280 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop  50 lit alloc dup kscd !  14 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop ;
: kcent ( i -- e )  50 lit * kscr @ + ;
: kwent ( i -- e )  6 lit lshift kswt @ + ;

\ ── checks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ kok? ( ptr len -- flag )  inside the requester's own region or its process's
: kok?  kst @ -rot tin? ;
: kh? ( ch -- flag )  ks2 @ 1 lit = ks1 @ c@ rot = and ;             \ is the key that one handle character
: kbnd ( -- key klen )  kst @ rrec dup 20 lit + swap 18 lit + @ ;     \ the output binding
: kibnd ( -- key klen )  kst @ rrec dup 288 lit + swap 284 lit + @ ;   \ the input binding
: kqb variable ;  : kqm variable ;
: kkeq ( a n b m -- flag )  kqm ! kqb !  dup kqm @ <> if 2drop 0 lit else -1 lit swap ?dup if 0 lit do over i + c@ kqb @ i + c@ <> if drop 0 lit then loop then nip then ;
: kcwd ( tid -- addr )  rrec 80 lit + ;                                \ the working directory: +0 length, +4 the bytes
\ kcur ( key klen -- addr )  the key's input cursor (made at 0 when there is none; a
\ scratch cell when the table is full), shared by every thread reading the key
: kcur
	0 lit 20 lit 0 lit do
		dup 0= if
			i kcent dup @ if dup 8 lit + over @ 5 lit pick 5 lit pick kkeq if nip else drop then else drop then
		then
	loop
	dup 0= if drop                                                   \ none: make one
		0 lit 20 lit 0 lit do dup 0= if i kcent @ 0= if drop i kcent then then loop
		?dup if rot over 8 lit + 3 lit pick mcopy  tuck !  0 lit over 4 lit + !  0 lit over 48 lit + ! else 2drop kscd @ then
	else nip nip then
	4 lit + ;
: kcurf ( key klen -- )  kcur 0 lit over !  -1 lit swap 44 lit + ! ;     \ rewound, and a file: its readers see its end
: kcurdel ( key klen -- )  20 lit 0 lit do i kcent dup @ if dup 8 lit + over @ 4 lit pick 4 lit pick kkeq if 0 lit over ! then then drop loop 2drop ;

\ ── paths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ kresv ( a n -- a' n' -1 | 0 )  the key as the tree sees it, in ksk: from the
\ root if it starts with "/", else under the requester's working directory;
\ 0 if that is over 511 bytes
: kresv
	dup if over c@ '/' lit = else 0 lit then if
		1 lit - swap 1 lit + swap  ksk @ ksp !
	else
		kst @ kcwd @ 1 lit - dup 0< if drop 0 lit then ?dup if
			kst @ kcwd 5 lit + ksk @ 2 lit pick mcopy  ksk @ + dup ksp ! '/' lit swap c!  ksp @ 1 lit + ksp !
		else ksk @ ksp ! then
	then
	ksp @ ksk @ - over + 1FF lit u> if 2drop 0 lit else
		2dup ksp @ swap mcopy  ksp @ + ksk @ - nip  ksk @ swap -1 lit then ;
: kres ( -- flag )  ks1 @ ks2 @ kresv if ks2 ! ks1 ! -1 lit else 0 lit then ;

\ ── events ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ kwake ( key klen -- )  a key was written: a thread whose input is bound to it
\ and waits for it is served again this turn; a thread watching it is posted
: kwk variable ;  : kwl variable ;
: kwake
	kwl ! kwk !
	10 lit 1 lit do
		i rrec 7C lit + @ 1 lit =  i ksbuf 40C lit + @ and if
			i rrec 288 lit + i rrec 284 lit + @ kwk @ kwl @ kkeq if -1 lit ksagain ! then
		then
	loop
	20 lit 0 lit do
		i kwent dup @ if dup 8 lit + over 4 lit + @ kwk @ kwl @ kkeq if 100000 lit over @ kpostd then then drop
	loop ;
: kwclear ( tid -- )  20 lit 0 lit do i kwent dup @ 2 lit pick = if 0 lit over ! then drop loop drop ;
: kwsweep ( -- )  20 lit 0 lit do i kwent dup @ ?dup if ktstate 0= if 0 lit over ! then then drop loop ;

\ ── the console ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
: kfn variable ;
: kflush ( tid -- )                               \ what is buffered to the bound key, or the UART; bytes a trap adds meanwhile (kuart) stay
	dup ksbuf 400 lit + @ dup 0= if 2drop else kfn !
		dup rrec 18 lit + @ if
			-1 lit txbeg dup 2 lit pick rrec dup 20 lit + swap 18 lit + @ 4 lit pick ksbuf kfn @ append txcommit
			dup rrec dup 20 lit + swap 18 lit + @ kwake
		else
			kfn @ ?dup if 0 lit do dup ksbuf i + c@ putc loop then                       \ unbound: the console is the UART
		then
		int_off
		dup ksbuf 400 lit + @ kfn @ - ?dup if
			over ksbuf kfn @ + 2 lit pick ksbuf 2 lit pick mcopy  over ksbuf 400 lit + !
		else 0 lit over ksbuf 400 lit + ! then
		int_on drop
	then ;

: kcput ( -- r )                                  \ bytes to the console or the bound key
	kst @ rrec 18 lit + @ 0= if
		ks4 @ ?dup if 0 lit do ks3 @ i + c@ putc loop then 0 lit
	else
		ks4 @ 400 lit kst @ ksbuf 400 lit + @ - u> if kst @ kflush then
		ks4 @ 400 lit u> if
			-1 lit txbeg dup kbnd ks3 @ ks4 @ append txcommit  kbnd kwake
		else
			kst @ ksbuf 400 lit + @ 0= if tms kst @ ksbuf 404 lit + ! then
			ks3 @ kst @ ksbuf dup 400 lit + @ + ks4 @ mcopy
			kst @ ksbuf 400 lit + dup @ ks4 @ + swap !
		then 0 lit
	then ;

: kcget ( -- r )                                  \ -3: nothing to read yet; the request stays pending and is served when there is
	kst @ rrec 284 lit + @ if
		kst @ kflush
		kibnd kcur ksp !
		0 lit txbeg dup kibnd ksp @ @ ks3 @ ks4 @ getat swap txcommit
		dup 0< if drop 0 lit else ksp @ @ - dup 0< if drop 0 lit then ks4 @ umin then
		?dup 0= if ksp @ 44 lit + @ if 0 lit else -1 lit kst @ ksbuf 40C lit + !  -3 lit then else dup ksp @ dup @ rot + swap ! then
	else
		10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and 0= if -1 lit kst @ ksbuf 40C lit + !  -1 lit ksuw !  -3 lit else
			0 lit begin dup ks4 @ u<  10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and  and while
				10000000 lit c@ over ks3 @ + c!  1 lit +
			repeat
		then
	then ;

: kbind ( -- r )                                  \ put on "1": where 0's output goes, a key resolved like any other
	ks4 @ 0= if kst @ kflush  0 lit kst @ rrec 18 lit + !  0 lit else
	ks3 @ ks4 @ kresv 0= if -1 lit else
		dup 3F lit u> if 2drop -2 lit else
			kst @ kflush
			2dup kst @ rrec 20 lit + swap mcopy  kst @ rrec 18 lit + ! drop  0 lit
		then
	then then ;
: kibind ( -- r )                                 \ put on "2": where 0's input comes from
	ks4 @ 0= if 0 lit kst @ rrec 284 lit + !  0 lit else
	ks3 @ ks4 @ kresv 0= if -1 lit else
		dup 3F lit u> if 2drop -2 lit else
			2dup kst @ rrec 288 lit + swap mcopy  kst @ rrec 284 lit + ! drop  0 lit
		then
	then then ;
: kcd ( -- r )                                    \ put on ".": the working directory, "/..." without a trailing slash
	ks4 @ 1 lit u> if ks3 @ ks4 @ + 1 lit - c@ '/' lit = if ks4 @ 1 lit - ks4 ! then then
	ks4 @ 0= ks4 @ 1FF lit u> or if -1 lit else ks3 @ c@ '/' lit <> if -1 lit else
		ks3 @ kst @ kcwd 4 lit + ks4 @ mcopy  ks4 @ kst @ kcwd !  0 lit then then ;

\ ── the ops ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
: kget ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? ks3 @ ks4 @ kok? and 0= if -2 lit else
		'0' lit kh? if kcget else
		'1' lit kh? if kbnd swap ks3 @ 2 lit pick ks4 @ umin mcopy else
		'2' lit kh? if kibnd swap ks3 @ 2 lit pick ks4 @ umin mcopy else
		'.' lit kh? if kst @ kcwd 4 lit + ks3 @ kst @ kcwd @ ks4 @ umin mcopy  kst @ kcwd @ else
		kres 0= if -1 lit else
		ks1 @ ks2 @ "proc/self/args" E lit kkeq if kst @ rrec 300 lit + ks3 @ kst @ rrec 2FC lit + @ ks4 @ umin mcopy  kst @ rrec 2FC lit + @ else
		0 lit txbeg dup ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ ks4 @ get swap txcommit then then then then then then
	then ;
: kput ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? ks3 @ ks4 @ kok? and 0= if -2 lit else
		'0' lit kh? if kcput else
		'1' lit kh? if kbind else
		'2' lit kh? if kibind else
		'.' lit kh? if kcd else
		kres 0= if -1 lit else
		ks1 @ ks2 @ "proc/self/args" E lit kkeq if ks4 @ FF lit u> if -1 lit else ks3 @ kst @ rrec 300 lit + ks4 @ mcopy  ks4 @ kst @ rrec 2FC lit + !  0 lit then else
		-1 lit txbeg dup ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ ks4 @ put txcommit  ks1 @ ks2 @ kcurdel  ks1 @ ks2 @ kwake  0 lit then then then then then then
	then ;
: kadd ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? ks3 @ ks4 @ kok? and 0= if -2 lit else
		'0' lit kh? if kcput else
		'1' lit kh? if kbind else
		'2' lit kh? '.' lit kh? or if -2 lit else
		kres 0= if -1 lit else -1 lit txbeg dup ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ ks4 @ append txcommit  ks1 @ ks2 @ kwake  0 lit then then then then
	then ;
: kdel ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else
		'0' lit kh? '1' lit kh? or '2' lit kh? or '.' lit kh? or if -2 lit else
		kres 0= if 0 lit else
		-1 lit txbeg dup ks1 @ ks2 @ del dup if swap txcommit ks1 @ ks2 @ kcurdel else swap txabort then then then
	then ;
: kexec ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else
		0 lit ks2 @ ?dup if 0 lit do ks1 @ i + c@ '/' lit = if drop -1 lit then loop then
		0= if                                                             \ a bare name: bin/NAME
			ks2 @ 1FB lit u> if 0 lit else "bin/" ksk @ 4 lit mcopy  ks1 @ ksk @ 4 lit + ks2 @ mcopy  ks2 @ 4 lit + ks2 !  ksk @ ks1 !  -1 lit then
		else kres then
		0= if 0 lit else
			kst @ rrec 18 lit + 0 lit rrec 18 lit + 48 lit mcopy             \ the child inherits from the spawner (thread 0): lend it the requester's binding
			kst @ rrec 80 lit + 0 lit rrec 80 lit + 380 lit mcopy             \ working directory, input binding, arguments
			ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ ks4 @ exec
			0 lit 0 lit rrec 18 lit + !  0 lit 0 lit rrec 284 lit + !  0 lit 0 lit rrec 2FC lit + !  1 lit 0 lit rrec 80 lit + !  '/' lit 0 lit rrec 84 lit + c!
		then
	then ;

: kread ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? ks3 @ C lit kok? and 0= if -2 lit else
		ks3 @ @ ks3 @ 4 lit + @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else
		kres 0= if -1 lit else
			0 lit txbeg dup ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ 8 lit + @ ks3 @ @ ks3 @ 4 lit + @ getat swap txcommit
			dup 0< 0= if ks3 @ 8 lit + @ - dup 0< if drop 0 lit then ks3 @ 4 lit + @ umin then
		then then
	then ;
: kwatch ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else kres 0= if -1 lit else ks2 @ 38 lit u> if -1 lit else
		0 lit 20 lit 0 lit do dup 0= if i kwent @ 0= if drop i kwent then then loop
		?dup 0= if -1 lit else kst @ over !  ks2 @ over 4 lit + !  ks1 @ over 8 lit + ks2 @ mcopy  drop 0 lit then
	then then then ;
: kunwtch ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else kres 0= if -1 lit else
		20 lit 0 lit do i kwent dup @ kst @ = if dup 8 lit + over 4 lit + @ ks1 @ ks2 @ kkeq if 0 lit over ! then then drop loop  0 lit
	then then ;
: kkillop ( -- r )
	ks1 @ F lit and dup 0= over kst @ = or if drop -2 lit else
		dup ktstate 0= if drop -1 lit else
			dup kkill  dup kflush  0 lit over rrec 18 lit + !  dup pgone  kwclear  0 lit
		then
	then ;
: krewind ( -- r )  ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? 0= if -2 lit else kres 0= if -1 lit else ks1 @ ks2 @ kcurf 0 lit then then ;
: kfill ( -- r )                                  \ op 10: the input buffer from the thread's input (kuart's reads), as kcget would
	kst @ rrec 284 lit + @ if
		kst @ kflush
		kibnd kcur ksp !
		0 lit txbeg dup kibnd ksp @ @ kst @ ksbuf 418 lit + 400 lit getat swap txcommit
		dup 0< if drop 0 lit else ksp @ @ - dup 0< if drop 0 lit then 400 lit umin then
		?dup 0= if ksp @ 44 lit + @ if -1 lit kst @ ksbuf 414 lit + !  0 lit else -1 lit kst @ ksbuf 40C lit + !  -3 lit then
		else dup ksp @ dup @ rot + swap !  dup kst @ ksbuf 408 lit + !  0 lit kst @ ksbuf 410 lit + ! then
	else
		10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and 0= if -1 lit kst @ ksbuf 40C lit + !  -1 lit ksuw !  -3 lit else
			0 lit begin dup 400 lit u<  10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and  and while 10000000 lit c@ over kst @ ksbuf 418 lit + + c!  1 lit + repeat
			dup kst @ ksbuf 408 lit + !  0 lit kst @ ksbuf 410 lit + !
		then
	then ;
: kflop ( -- r )  kst @ kflush  0 lit ;           \ op 11: the output buffer out (kuart's writes)
: khalt? ( -- r )  bye 0 lit ;                      \ op 12: the node halts (the machine stops: scripts/boot.sh returns)
: kbindp ( -- r )  kst @ ks1 @ ks2 @ ks3 @ ks4 @ pbind ;
: kunbind ( -- r )  kst @ ks1 @ ks2 @ punbind 0 lit ;
: ktxring ( -- r )  kst @ ks1 @ ks2 @ ptxset ;
: knetinf ( -- r )
	ks1 @ 18 lit kok? 0= if -2 lit else
		ipaddr @ ks1 @ !  ipmask @ ks1 @ 4 lit + !  ipgw @ ks1 @ 8 lit + !
		ipgw @ arpfind ?dup if 4 lit + ks1 @ C lit + 6 lit mcopy else 6 lit 0 lit do 0 lit ks1 @ C lit + i + c! loop then
		netmac ks1 @ 12 lit + 6 lit mcopy  0 lit
	then ;

: ksu variable ;  : ksx variable ;  : ksn variable ;  : ksq variable ;
\ ksrec? ( -- flag )  the cursor's key and value as a record, if it fits: written if so
: kskl variable ;  : ksvl variable ;  : kssz variable ;
: ksrec?
	ksu @ 0 lit ksbuf 200 lit curkey kskl !
	ksu @ 0 lit ksbuf 200 lit + 40 lit curval ksvl !
	kskl @ 3 lit + FFFFFFFC lit and  ksvl @ 40 lit umin 3 lit + FFFFFFFC lit and + 8 lit + kssz !
	ksq @ kssz @ + ks3 @ ks4 @ + u> if 0 lit else
		kskl @ ksq @ !  ksvl @ ksq @ 4 lit + !
		0 lit ksbuf ksq @ 8 lit + kskl @ mcopy
		0 lit ksbuf 200 lit + ksq @ 8 lit + kskl @ 3 lit + FFFFFFFC lit and + ksvl @ 40 lit umin mcopy
		ksq @ kssz @ + ksq !  -1 lit
	then ;
: kscan ( -- r )
	ks1 @ ks2 @ kok? ks3 @ ks4 @ kok? and ks2 @ 1FF lit u> 0= and 0= if -2 lit else
		kres 0= if -1 lit else
			0 lit txbeg ksx !  ksx @ curopen ksu !
			ks2 @ if ksu @ ks1 @ ks2 @ curseek drop else ksu @ curfirst drop then
			ks3 @ ksq !  0 lit ksn !
			begin ksu @ 4 lit + @ if ksrec? else 0 lit then while
				ksn @ 1 lit + ksn !  ksu @ curnext drop
			repeat
			ksu @ curclose  ksx @ txcommit  ksn @
		then
	then ;

: kserve ( tid -- )
	dup kst !  rrec dup 64 lit + @ kso !  dup 68 lit + @ ks1 !  dup 6C lit + @ ks2 !  dup 70 lit + @ ks3 !  74 lit + @ ks4 !
	0 lit kst @ ksbuf 40C lit + !
	kso @ 1 lit = if kget else kso @ 2 lit = if kput else kso @ 3 lit = if kadd else
	kso @ 4 lit = if kdel else kso @ 5 lit = if kexec else kso @ 6 lit = if kbindp else
	kso @ 7 lit = if kunbind else kso @ 8 lit = if ktxring else kso @ 9 lit = if knetinf else
	kso @ A lit = if kscan else kso @ B lit = if kread else kso @ C lit = if kwatch else
	kso @ D lit = if kunwtch else kso @ E lit = if kkillop else kso @ F lit = if krewind else
	kso @ 10 lit = if kfill else kso @ 11 lit = if kflop else kso @ 12 lit = if khalt? else -2 lit
	then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then then
	dup -3 lit = if drop else
		kst @ rrec dup 78 lit + rot swap !  2 lit swap 7C lit + !  20000 lit kst @ kpostd
	then ;

: kssw variable ;
: ksturn ( -- )
	0 lit ksuw !
	begin
		0 lit ksagain !
		10 lit 1 lit do
			i ptxdrain
			i rrec 7C lit + @ 1 lit = if i kserve then
			i ksbuf 400 lit + @ if
				i ktstate 0=  i ksbuf 400 lit + @ 400 lit = or  tms i ksbuf 404 lit + @ - 64 lit u< 0= or  if i kflush then
			then
		loop
	ksagain @ 0= until                                                 \ a write woke a reader: serve it now
	tms kssw @ - 3E8 lit u< 0= if tms kssw ! psweep kwsweep then ;   \ the sweep once a second

\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ Tests (the store open, sds): every op as if thread 15 had asked, with a
\ buffer standing in for its region; then a user thread that really asks,
\ through the syscalls, for a put.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Test {
	ksops {
		: kbuf variable ;
		: kreqf ( op a b c d -- r )
			F lit rrec 74 lit + !  F lit rrec 70 lit + !  F lit rrec 6C lit + !  F lit rrec 68 lit + !  F lit rrec 64 lit + !
			1 lit F lit rrec 7C lit + !  F lit kserve
			F lit rrec 7C lit + @ 2 lit = if F lit rrec 78 lit + @ else -3 lit then ;
		: kcmp ( a s n -- flag )  -1 lit swap 0 lit do 2 lit pick i + c@ 2 lit pick i + c@ <> if drop 0 lit then loop nip nip ;
		sds @ if
			ksinit
			1000 lit alloc kbuf !  kbuf @ F lit rrec !  1000 lit F lit rrec 4 lit + !  0 lit F lit rrec 18 lit + !
			1 lit F lit rrec 80 lit + !  '/' lit F lit rrec 84 lit + c!                                   \ F works at the root
			"ks/a" kbuf @ 4 lit mcopy  "hi" kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit mcopy  '0' lit kbuf @ 20 lit + c!  '1' lit kbuf @ 21 lit + c!
			"ks/log" kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit mcopy
			2 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                              \ put
			1 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 2 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hi" 2 lit kcmp assert
			3 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 1 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                              \ append "h"
			1 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 3 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hih" 3 lit kcmp assert
			4 lit kbuf @ 4 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq  4 lit kbuf @ 4 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit sbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                           \ a kernel pointer
			1 lit kbuf @ 4 lit kbuf @ FFF lit + 40 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                            \ runs past the region
			9 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                                         \ no such op
			\ handles: bind 0 to ks/log, write, flush, read it back through 0
			2 lit kbuf @ 21 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 21 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 6 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "ks/log" 6 lit kcmp assert
			2 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ "hi": buffered
			F lit ksbuf 400 lit + @ 2 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq                   \ not in the store yet
			F lit kflush  F lit ksbuf 400 lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 2 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hi" 2 lit kcmp assert
			3 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 1 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ "h" again, buffered
			'2' lit kbuf @ 23 lit + c!
			2 lit kbuf @ 23 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ and read 0 from ks/log: a pipe to itself
			1 lit kbuf @ 23 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 6 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "ks/log" 6 lit kcmp assert
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 3 lit kreqf 3 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hih" 3 lit kcmp assert   \ reading 0 flushes the output, then reads the input from its cursor
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -3 lit asrt_eq                   \ at its end: pending until it grows
			F lit ksbuf 40C lit + @ 0 lit <> assert  0 lit F lit rrec 7C lit + !
			2 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ "hi" out, buffered
			2 lit kbuf @ 21 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                               \ output back to the console: flushed
			F lit rrec 18 lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 5 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hihhi" 5 lit kcmp assert
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 2 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hi" 2 lit kcmp assert   \ the input grew: what is past the cursor
			F lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                                \ rewind ks/log, now a file
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 5 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "hihhi" 5 lit kcmp assert
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                    \ at its end: 0, not pending
			F lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf drop
			10 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 5 lit asrt_eq  F lit ksbuf 418 lit + "hihhi" 5 lit kcmp assert   \ the emulated UART's input buffer
			10 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  F lit ksbuf 414 lit + @ 0 lit <> assert          \ and its end
			0 lit F lit ksbuf 414 lit + !  0 lit F lit ksbuf 408 lit + !
			2 lit kbuf @ 23 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                               \ input back to the console
			F lit rrec 284 lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -3 lit asrt_eq                   \ console input: nothing yet, pending
			F lit rrec 7C lit + @ 1 lit asrt_eq  0 lit F lit rrec 7C lit + !  ksuw @ 0 lit <> assert
			\ the arguments: a line kept in the record
			"/proc/self/args" kbuf @ 70 lit + F lit mcopy  "cat a b" kbuf @ 80 lit + 7 lit mcopy
			2 lit kbuf @ 70 lit + F lit kbuf @ 80 lit + 7 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq
			1 lit kbuf @ 70 lit + F lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 7 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "cat a b" 7 lit kcmp assert
			2 lit kbuf @ 70 lit + F lit kbuf @ 80 lit + 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  F lit rrec 2FC lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq
			\ watch, read at an offset, kill
			C lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                                \ watch ks/log
			0 lit F lit tcb 9C lit + !
			2 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ a put to it: posted bit 20
			F lit tcb 9C lit + @ 100000 lit and 0 lit <> assert  0 lit F lit tcb 9C lit + !
			D lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                                \ unwatch
			2 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 2 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  F lit tcb 9C lit + @ 100000 lit and 0 lit asrt_eq
			kbuf @ 100 lit + kbuf @ 300 lit + !  2 lit kbuf @ 304 lit + !  1 lit kbuf @ 308 lit + !
			B lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 300 lit + 0 lit kreqf 1 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + c@ 'i' lit asrt_eq   \ "hi" from 1: "i"
			5 lit kbuf @ 308 lit + !  B lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 300 lit + 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq             \ past the end
			E lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                                           \ kill: not thread 0
			E lit F lit 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                                           \ nor oneself
			\ the network: a port held through a ring in the region, the addresses, a frame out
			4 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + !  604 lit kbuf @ 20C lit + !
			6 lit 11 lit 1F91 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + E00 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq                   \ 0x1810 does not fit 0xE00
			6 lit 11 lit 1F91 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + E00 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq
			2 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + !
			6 lit 11 lit 1F91 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + E00 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  11 lit 1F91 lit pfind 8 lit + @ F lit asrt_eq
			6 lit 11 lit 1F91 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + E00 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq
			7 lit 11 lit 1F91 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  11 lit 1F91 lit pfind 0 lit asrt_eq
			9 lit kbuf @ 800 lit + 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 800 lit + @ ipaddr @ asrt_eq
			kbuf @ 812 lit + netmac 6 lit kcmp assert
			8 lit kbuf @ 200 lit + E00 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq  F lit ptx @ kbuf @ 200 lit + asrt_eq
			8 lit sbuf @ E00 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -2 lit asrt_eq
			0 lit F lit ptx !
			\ scan: three keys under ks/s, two records fit a small buffer, all three (and whatever follows) a large one
			"ks/s/a" kbuf @ 6 lit mcopy  "ks/s/b" kbuf @ 8 lit + 6 lit mcopy  "ks/s/c" kbuf @ 10 lit + 6 lit mcopy  "ks/s" kbuf @ 18 lit + 4 lit mcopy
			"one" kbuf @ 20 lit + 3 lit mcopy  "twotwotwo" kbuf @ 30 lit + 9 lit mcopy
			2 lit kbuf @ 6 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 3 lit kreqf drop  2 lit kbuf @ 8 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 9 lit kreqf drop  2 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 20 lit + 0 lit kreqf drop
			A lit kbuf @ 18 lit + 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 100 lit kreqf 2 lit u> assert
			kbuf @ 100 lit + @ 6 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 104 lit + @ 3 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 108 lit + "ks/s/a" 6 lit kcmp assert  kbuf @ 110 lit + "one" 3 lit kcmp assert
			kbuf @ 114 lit + @ 6 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 118 lit + @ 9 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 11C lit + "ks/s/b" 6 lit kcmp assert  kbuf @ 124 lit + "twotwotwo" 9 lit kcmp assert
			kbuf @ 130 lit + @ 6 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 134 lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 138 lit + "ks/s/c" 6 lit kcmp assert
			A lit kbuf @ 18 lit + 4 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 30 lit kreqf 2 lit asrt_eq                   \ the third does not fit 0x30
			A lit kbuf @ 8 lit + 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 100 lit kreqf 0 lit u> assert  kbuf @ 108 lit + "ks/s/b" 6 lit kcmp assert   \ from a key: that key first
			A lit kbuf @ 30 lit + 2 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 100 lit kreqf drop                           \ "tw": whatever follows it
			\ the working directory: "." is "/" to begin with; relative keys resolve under it, absolute ones from the root
			'.' lit kbuf @ 22 lit + c!  "/ks/s/" kbuf @ 40 lit + 6 lit mcopy  'a' lit kbuf @ 50 lit + c!  "nope" kbuf @ 58 lit + 4 lit mcopy  "/ks/s/a" kbuf @ 60 lit + 7 lit mcopy
			1 lit kbuf @ 22 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 1 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + c@ '/' lit asrt_eq
			2 lit kbuf @ 22 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 58 lit + 4 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq                     \ no leading slash: refused
			2 lit kbuf @ 22 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 40 lit + 6 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ cd /ks/s/ (the slash dropped)
			1 lit kbuf @ 22 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 5 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "/ks/s" 5 lit kcmp assert
			1 lit kbuf @ 50 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 3 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ 100 lit + "one" 3 lit kcmp assert   \ "a" is ks/s/a here
			1 lit kbuf @ 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq                            \ "ks/s/a" is ks/s/ks/s/a here: nothing
			1 lit kbuf @ 60 lit + 7 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 3 lit asrt_eq                    \ "/ks/s/a" is absolute
			A lit kbuf @ 50 lit + 0 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 100 lit kreqf 0 lit u> assert  kbuf @ 108 lit + "ks/s/a" 6 lit kcmp assert   \ a scan from "" starts at the directory
			2 lit kbuf @ 22 lit + 1 lit kbuf @ 40 lit + 1 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                      \ cd /
			1 lit kbuf @ 6 lit kbuf @ 100 lit + 40 lit kreqf 3 lit asrt_eq
			4 lit kbuf @ 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf drop  4 lit kbuf @ 8 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf drop  4 lit kbuf @ 10 lit + 6 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf drop
			-1 lit txbeg dup "ks/log" 6 lit del drop txcommit
			0 lit F lit rrec !  0 lit F lit rrec 4 lit + !
		then
	}
	\ a user thread that asks, through the syscalls, for "xyz" to be put under "k",
	\ keeps the reply and sleeps so the test can look
	ksreq {
		: rxi variable ;  : kt0 variable ;
		sds @ if
			110 lit alloc rxi !  rxi @ 44 lit pgzero
			FEC10113 lit rxi @ !  00200293 lit rxi @ 4 lit + !  00512823 lit rxi @ 8 lit + !  10080293 lit rxi @ C lit + !
			00512623 lit rxi @ 10 lit + !  00100293 lit rxi @ 14 lit + !  00512423 lit rxi @ 18 lit + !  10480293 lit rxi @ 1C lit + !
			00512223 lit rxi @ 20 lit + !  00300293 lit rxi @ 24 lit + !  00512023 lit rxi @ 28 lit + !  00D00893 lit rxi @ 2C lit + !
			00000073 lit rxi @ 30 lit + !  00410113 lit rxi @ 34 lit + !  00E00893 lit rxi @ 38 lit + !  00000073 lit rxi @ 3C lit + !
			00012283 lit rxi @ 40 lit + !  00410113 lit rxi @ 44 lit + !
			00001337 lit rxi @ 48 lit + !  01030333 lit rxi @ 4C lit + !  00532023 lit rxi @ 50 lit + !   \ the reply to a6 + 0x1000
			000F42B7 lit rxi @ 54 lit + !  24028293 lit rxi @ 58 lit + !  FFC10113 lit rxi @ 5C lit + !  00512023 lit rxi @ 60 lit + !
			00400893 lit rxi @ 64 lit + !  00000073 lit rxi @ 68 lit + !  00100893 lit rxi @ 6C lit + !  00000073 lit rxi @ 70 lit + !
			'k' lit rxi @ 100 lit + c!  "xyz" rxi @ 104 lit + 3 lit mcopy
			-1 lit txbeg dup "bin/r" 5 lit rxi @ 108 lit put txcommit
			"bin/r" 5 lit 20000 lit 5 lit exec dup 0 lit <> assert kt0 !
			begin ksturn yield kt0 @ tstate 2 lit = until                   \ served, and asleep after it
			kt0 @ rrec @ 1000 lit + @ 0 lit asrt_eq                         \ the reply
			0 lit txbeg dup "k" 1 lit kbuf @ 40 lit get 3 lit asrt_eq  kbuf @ "xyz" 3 lit kcmp assert  txcommit
			0 lit rfree xr0 !
			E lit kt0 @ 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf 0 lit asrt_eq                                            \ killed (by F): gone, code 9, its region back
			kt0 @ tstate 0 lit asrt_eq  kt0 @ texcode 9 lit asrt_eq  0 lit rfree xr0 @ 1 lit + asrt_eq
			E lit kt0 @ 0 lit 0 lit 0 lit kreqf -1 lit asrt_eq
			-1 lit txbeg dup "k" 1 lit del drop dup "bin/r" 5 lit del drop txcommit
		then
	}
}
